@@s021 In-class test: two attempts, then no more
@@s022 "Students have two attempts to pass each in-class test… Students who do not complete and pass an in-class test after both attempts are not eligible to take the exam." If you miss the first, the second is held one or two weeks later, outside the lecture time. It covers the material of the previous weeks: for the first, the pages of weeks 1–5 of this atlas.
@@s023 Presentations
@@s024 If a student does not show up or has not really tried to solve the assigned exercise, the group is given another exercise to present (official description).
@@s025 What is expected from the assignments
@@s026 "Assignments are <b>not</b> expected to be flawless." They ask instead for:
@@s027 <b>An honest attempt</b>: an honest attempt.
@@s028 <b>Reproducibility</b>: a TA or a classmate must understand how you obtained the results (method, parameters, reasoning, code).
@@s029 <b>Reflection</b>: interpreting and discussing the results, why a method worked or not, limits, alternatives.
@@s030 <b>Understanding of the underlying theory</b>: how the theory connects to the problem, without copying the course material.
@@s031 If an assignment is not handed in or is not sufficient, there is one more week to hand it in again. The assignments and the exercises are also <b>exam material</b>: the oral starts from there.
@@s032 AI, collaboration, group
@@s033 During the course
@@s034 Generative AI is allowed as support for study, exercises and assignments. But you must be able to explain methods and results in your own words, because at the oral they will ask exactly about those.
@@s035 At the exam
@@s036 "No use of generative artificial intelligence is allowed at the exam under any circumstances."
@@s037 Discussing and collaborating is encouraged. If someone has contributed substantially, one line in the notebook is enough ("Developed together with…").
@@s038 All members of the group must take part and understand the work handed in. If a member does not contribute, it must be reported to the course coordinator.
@@s039 Stuck for more than about an hour on an exercise? Ask the TAs.
